@namespace IzzyBlazor
@typeparam TValue
@inherits MonthYearFieldBase<TValue>
@attribute [ModeSupport(NoScript = ModeLevel.Partial, NoScriptNotes = "With JavaScript off, it's the browser's own month input, a text box taking YYYY-MM where the browser has none.")]

@*
    A month field, such as a card's expiry: the month is held as the 1st of it, in a DateOnly or
    DateTime, or a nullable one. A page of twelve months opens to choose from.

    On a desktop a month is chosen, not typed, and its button shows it, since browsers other than
    Chromium's have no month input. A phone and UseNative keep the browser's input, and with no script
    it's the browser's too, a text box with a pattern where it has none. Min and Max compare whole
    months, so a Min of March 15 allows March. [Range] compares the 1st of the month, so give it a
    1st, as a Range starting on March 15 would turn away March.

    Accessibility:
    - The month's button stands in for the input on a desktop, so it's named by the field's label and
      the month, and takes the hint and errors.
    - The page of months is a `grid`, named by its year, with the chosen month's `aria-selected` and
      this month's `aria-current`. Focus goes to the chosen month or this one, and on closing back to
      the button.
    - Label, hint and errors work as in `TextField`.

    Keyboard:
    In the month field
    - Alt+Down | Open the months
    In the page of months
    - Left, Right | Move a month (reversed in right-to-left)
    - Up, Down | Move a row
    - Home, End | Go to the start or end of the row
    - Page Up, Page Down | Move a year
    - Enter, Space | Choose it and close
    - Tab, Shift+Tab | Move through the header and the months, and close past either end
    - Escape | Close without changing the value
    See also: YearField, DateField, Calendar.
*@

@{ base.BuildRenderTree(__builder); }

@code {
    /// <inheritdoc />
    private protected override bool IsYear => false;

    /// <inheritdoc />
    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (Underlying != typeof(DateOnly) && Underlying != typeof(DateTime))
        {
            throw new InvalidOperationException($"MonthField holds the 1st of a month, so bind it to DateOnly or DateTime, or a nullable one, not {typeof(TValue)}.");
        }

        base.OnParametersSet();
    }
}
